.TH PRR 1 "October 2026" "prr 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prr \- review Gitea pull requests with Claude
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prr serve
.RB [ \-\-addr
.IR host:port ]
.br
.B prr mcp
.br
.B prr setup
.RB [ \-\-global ]
.br
.B prr check
.br
.B prr version
.br
.B prr help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prr
connects Claude Code to a Gitea server so that pull requests can be reviewed
from the Claude Code prompt.
It is an MCP server: Claude calls its tools to list repositories and pull
requests, read the annotated diff and any file in the repository, record
findings, and post the review with inline comments.
Everything Claude does is written to a session file per pull request and
shown on a web dashboard, together with the live state of the review on
Gitea: which inline comments the author has resolved, what was pushed since,
CI status and whether the pull request was merged.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Start the dashboard at
.B http://ADDR/
and the MCP endpoint at
.BR http://ADDR/mcp .
Register the endpoint once with
.B claude mcp add \-\-transport http prr http://127.0.0.1:8787/mcp
and it is available in every Claude Code session while
.B serve
runs.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the MCP server on standard input and output.
This is the stdio transport for
.BR "claude mcp add prr \-\- prr mcp" .
It needs no running server but must be able to find the configuration;
set
.B PRR_ENV
to the path of the project
.I .env
when Claude Code is started from another directory.
.TP
.B setup
Ask for the Gitea URL and token and write them to
.I ./.env
(or, with
.BR \-\-global ,
to
.IR ~/.config/prr/config.env ).
The token is checked against Gitea before the next steps are printed.
.TP
.B check
Verify the Gitea connection and print which configuration file and data
directory are in use.
.SH TOOLS
The MCP tools, as Claude sees them.
Tools marked
.I write
change the pull request on Gitea; Claude Code asks before running them unless
told otherwise, and the server instructions tell Claude to post only when the
human asks.
.TP
.B list_repos
Repositories the token can see.
.TP
.B list_pulls
Pull requests in a repository.
.TP
.B get_pull
Metadata, description, changed files and the annotated diff of one pull
request.
Starts the session shown on the dashboard.
.TP
.B get_diff
The annotated diff of one changed file, for pull requests too large to inline.
.TP
.B read_file, list_dir
Read any file, or list any directory, at the head or base of the pull request.
.TP
.B get_comments
Reviews, inline comments and their resolved state, and the conversation
already on the pull request.
.TP
.B review_status
Which inline comments the author resolved, commits pushed since the review,
CI status and merge state.
.TP
.B note
Record a finding, summary, decision or question on the dashboard timeline.
.TP
.BR post_review " (write)"
Post a review with inline comments.
Every comment is given as fields and rendered the same way:
the issue in its simplest form, a copy-pasteable fix (a one-click Gitea
suggestion when it replaces exactly the commented line), why the fix is
right, and why the obvious alternative is not.
Comment positions are checked against the diff before anything is sent.
.TP
.BR post_comment " (write)"
Post a plain comment on the pull request conversation.
.SH DIFF FORMAT
Diffs are shown with two line-number columns followed by the usual marker:
.PP
.nf
  OLD   NEW |
   11     - |-  const b = 2;
    -    11 |+  const b = 3;
   12    13 |   return a + b;
.fi
.PP
The NEW column is the line number for added and context lines, the OLD column
for removed lines.
These are the numbers Gitea expects for inline comments.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read, lowest priority first, from
.IR ~/.config/prr/config.env ,
a
.I .env
next to the binary, the nearest
.I .env
in the current directory or a parent, the file named by
.BR PRR_ENV ,
and finally the environment.
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea server. Required.
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Access token from
.IR GITEA_URL/user/settings/applications .
Needs the scopes user (read), repository (read and write) and issue (read and
write).
Required.
.TP
.B PRR_ADDR
Listen address for
.BR serve .
Default 127.0.0.1:8787.
.TP
.B PRR_DATA
Directory for session files.
Default
.I data/
next to the
.I .env
that holds the token.
.TP
.B PRR_DIFF_LIMIT
Inline the whole diff in
.B get_pull
up to this many bytes; above it, Claude fetches files one by one with
.BR get_diff .
Default 120000.
.TP
.B PRR_ENV
Path of one more env file to read, with priority over the project
.IR .env .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.env
Project configuration, written by
.BR "prr setup" .
.TP
.I ./data/*.json
One session per pull request: tool calls, notes and posted reviews.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/prr.service
Installed by
.BR "install.sh \-\-service" .
.SH NOTES
Gitea refuses the APPROVED and REQUEST_CHANGES verdicts on a pull request
opened by the same account the token belongs to.
Use a separate reviewer account, or let
.B post_review
fall back to a COMMENT review with the verdict in the summary.
.PP
Links in Gitea API responses are built from the server's ROOT_URL setting;
.B prr
rewrites their origin to
.B GITEA_URL
so they work even when ROOT_URL is wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up and start:
.PP
.nf
  ./install.sh \-\-service
  prr check
.fi
.PP
In Claude Code:
.PP
.nf
  /review-pr baktash/nest-dokploy-demo#1
  post it
  what did the author fix since my review?
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claude (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
